#
# The Mali gate's settings. tools/check.sh reads this file at the Mali test
# row (it is bash, sourced). It lives under tools/mali so that a Mali change
# which edits it selects the mali scope only; in check.sh it would select
# every row (scope_of_path maps tools/check.sh to `all`).
#
# MALI_TEST_SOURCES: where the Mali tests are declared. The Mali test row
# (`cargo test --lib mali:: the_triangle_sample_shaders_build_on_the_mali`
# in the host-test,gpu-mali,shaderc-online,no-shader-table build) passes
# when the tests that passed are exactly the #[test] functions of these
# sources, none failed and none ignored (tests_as_declared in
# tools/check.sh; an entry is a directory, a file, or <file>#<item> for one
# inline module or one test of a file). So a Mali test that is no longer
# compiled, or that the filter no longer selects, turns the row red, and a
# change that adds or removes a test in these places edits nothing here.
# Add an entry only when Mali tests appear in a new place: the row then
# names each test that ran from a place this list does not have.
MALI_TEST_SOURCES=(
  src/mali
  src/shaderc/online/mali
  src/osal/mali.rs
  src/msaa_hw/mali.rs
  src/shaderc/online/backend.rs#mali
  src/shaderc/online/triangle_sample_tests.rs#the_triangle_sample_shaders_build_on_the_mali
)
